      "elapsedMs": 14906,
      "answer": "The stated fact is only \"We began development on August 23, 2026\", a date with no time or timezone. GIBC V2 Open Invention (rule gibc-start) requires development to begin after July 11, 2026 at 04:00 UTC and before the October 1, 2026 15:45 UTC deadline. August 23, 2026 falls inside that window, so the date alone does not conflict with the window; however, the rule's curated question asks for a timezone on the opening day, and no time or UTC offset was supplied, so the exact timestamp remains unknown and cannot be invented. My independent reading was \"unclear\" on gibc-start; the typed check returned \"supported\" for the supplied date. That disagreement is preserved here, and the typed result is authoritative for the report but is not organizer approval. Origin (gibc-origin) and prior-entry (gibc-previous-entry) facts are still missing. Next step: supply the start time with UTC offset, plus what existed before July 11 and whether this duplicates a prior hackathon entry.",
